# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Datasets (~4.7 GB) — UCSD, WSDOT night, UA-DETRAC, BMD-45, teammate videos.
# Re-obtain from the sources documented in the BASELINE_*.md reports.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
*.zip
*.tgz
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights (~395 MB). Stock YOLO weights download automatically on first
# run; the fine-tuned BMD-45 weights are reproducible via train_finetune.py.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pt
*.onnx
models/
runs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rendered media — annotated videos, calibration frames, preview stills.
# All regenerable by re-running the layer that produced them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.mp4
*.avi
*.mkv
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.gif

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bulk pipeline output.
#
# The per-clip batch directories hold one tracks CSV + JSON per clip across the
# 254-clip UCSD runs (~40 MB). They are raw output, not results: the findings
# that matter are already distilled into aggregate.json and the BASELINE_*.md
# reports, both of which are kept.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/*/
results_v11/*/
results_v11m/*/
results_night/*/

# The JSON tracks dump duplicates the CSV of the same name at ~4x the size.
# The CSV is the documented interchange format (see OUTPUT_FORMAT.md), so the
# JSON twin is redundant in version control.
*_tracks.json

# Screen-recording scratch from the violation feasibility scan; the conclusions
# live in VIOLATION_SCAN.md.
outputs_scan/Screen Recording*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Exploratory output folders.
#
# Scratch output from dataset evaluation and parameter sweeps that fed the
# reports but is not part of the working pipeline and is not needed by the
# downstream OCR module. Kept on local disk, untracked here. The conclusions
# drawn from each survive in the corresponding report.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: git only honours '#' as a comment at the START of a line, so each
# pattern below stands alone. A trailing comment would become part of the
# pattern and silently match nothing.

# first UCSD single-clip smoke test
outputs/
# UA-DETRAC evaluation, stock and fine-tuned
outputs_detrac/
outputs_detrac_ft/
# UCSD regression check on the fine-tuned weights
outputs_ucsd_ft/
# night sample clips and the conf/imgsz sweep -> BASELINE_NIGHT.md
outputs_night/
outputs_night_c02/
# violation feasibility scan -> VIOLATION_SCAN.md
outputs_scan/
# night batch aggregate -> BASELINE_NIGHT.md
results_night/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately KEPT, despite sitting next to the above:
#   outputs_calib/*.csv          reference outputs for all 4 violation layers
#   outputs_calib/*_meta.json    thresholds + assumptions behind every layer
#   outputs_demo/homography.*    site calibration (IRC-based)
#   outputs_demo/lanes.json      lane boundaries
#   outputs_demo/zones.json      carriageway zones
#   results/aggregate.json       YOLOv8s baseline — the v8 side of the v8-vs-v11
#                                comparison, so it stays with results_v11*/
#   results_v11/aggregate.json   YOLOv11s baseline, full 254 clips
#   results_v11m/batch_log.txt   YOLOv11m run log. NOTE: this run was stopped
#                                at clip 58/254 and never aggregated, so there
#                                is no aggregate.json for it and BASELINE_V11.md
#                                does not report v11m numbers.
#   results_generalisation/      evidence for KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md section 5
#                                (truck collapse, rickshaw hallucination)
#   results_val*.json            fine-tuning before/after numbers
# These are small and are what make the reports and the CSV schema verifiable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
